  abstract = {"A series of investigations was carried out to analyze the determinants of the difficulty of perceptual recall of a systematically varied set of stimuli. In Part I, the accuracy with which Ss could reproduce these arrays under .5-sec. exposure was determined. In Part II, another method involving discrimination between arrays yielded a similar ranking of accuracy scores." An analysis was constructed, based on the verbal-loop hypothesis that the Ss' perceptual processing includes a covert verbalization the length of which determines the difficulty of the stimulus for perceptual tasks. Empirically derived measures based on this hypothesis were shown to account for a major part of the variance in array difficulty. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)},
