  abstract = {According to M. Wertheimer (1959), the processes of productive thinking are determined by the nature of the inner structural requirements of the problem situation. A conflict can arise between the requirements of the goal and the requirements of the means at disposal for reaching the goal. This conflict generates strains from which vectors arise leading to productive restructurings. In the present paper some situations are examined in which the organizational tendencies inherent in the features of the material cause a premature solution, so that these tendencies can be considered as obstacles to the solution. Data from 40 Ss are included. (Italian summary) (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)},
